PARITY NOTES (vs web SummaryStatsRow.tsx)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Presentational row (props + useTranslation; NO data hooks) -> error/stale/offline are owned by the parent
  Security-Access page, exactly like the sibling ChartsRow/HighlightCard ports. The two states the web
  component itself renders are reproduced: Loading (4x Skeleton height=88, grid-cols-1/sm:2/lg:4) and Ready
  (FadeIn over 4 MetricCards). Documented in SummaryStatsRow.Model.cs.
* MetricCard -> TsMetricCard, Skeleton -> TsSkeleton, FadeIn -> TsFadeIn (the shared native counterparts).
  Web `icon`+`color` map to TsMetricCard's accent rail (it carries no glyph slot) -> the same mapping the
  sibling TemperatureMetricCards port uses. color tokens:
    secure=TsColorSuccessBrush(#10B981)  unsecure=TsColorDangerBrush(#EF4444)
    cyan=TsColorInfoBrush(#00F0FF, exact neon-cyan)  blue=TsChartSpeedBrush(#3B82F6)
    purple=TsChartPowerBrush(#A855F7, exact neon-purple)
* Values reproduce the web exactly: status secure/unsecure word; lastLock via helpers.ts timeSince
  (null/future -> em dash, <60s "just now", <60m "{n}m ago", <24h "{n}h ago", else "{n}d ago");
  sentryUptime via fmtInt (NumberFormatting.Format(_,null,0)) + "%"; totalEvents the verbatim integer.
* i18n: every source t() key used with the web fallback
  (admin.security.stat.status/secure/unsecure/stat.lastLock/stat.sentryUptime/stat.totalEvents,
  common.loading); timeSince's untranslated web literals routed through the facade
  (time.justNow/minutesAgo/hoursAgo/daysAgo, web literal as fallback) so no bare English sits in native code.
* Telemetry: SummaryStatsRowDiagnostics emits `view.opened slug=SummaryStatsRow`, PII-safe.

